  "body": "This is an independent audit of the written transfer lemmas in #1786 (chafreaky, \"Conditional \u03ba = 0.001679754788150048 from fine source-prime padding\"), at head `c52345caa318fc6b1b6e2659c57d746317a72823`. It answers that PR's Open next questions 1 and 2 for the explicit inequalities. **No gap was found in the audited scope. No new \u03ba is claimed, and the selected record is unchanged.**\n\nPackage: `research/pr1786-fine-prime-transfer-audit/`. The verifier is stdlib-only, runs in under one second, and is written from the prose. It neither imports nor reads #1786's checkers, `LEDGER.json` or `CLAIM.json`.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **\u00a71, prime interval.**\n   - The interval gives `1/(4p\u00b2) < \u03b8 \u2264 1/(2p\u00b2-1)`, and `S/T > 1/2` whenever `d \u2264 p`. Checked exactly for p = 2..2000.\n   - The Trudgian Theorem 2 step is sound. The main term is at least `\u03b7x/log x`, and the two endpoint errors total at most `2f(x)` because `f` is increasing.\n   - INFORMATIONAL: if `log x = c\u00b7p^(1-\u03b5)` at \u03b5 = 0.9999999, the bound becomes effective at `ln p \u2248 4.3\u00b710\u2078` (3.8\u20134.8\u00b710\u2078 for c from 100 to 0.01). This quantifies the cutoff the PR already disclaims.\n2. **\u00a72, conditioning.** The cited bounds do carry the \u03b8-dependence the transfer substitutes:\n   - PR1673 LOG-A \u00a71 holds for every \u03b8 > 0;\n   - FORWARD-SMALL-A \u00a71\u20132 is explicit for 0 < \u03b8 \u2264 1;\n   - PR1758's accretive gaps are \u2265 \u03b8/2 (narrow) and \u2265 \u03b8 (broad).\n\n   The new row margin `1/(8p\u00b2)` holds uniformly in p. A control shows the old `1/(8p)` margin fails at the new \u03b8. I also derived the **column** analogue that \u00a75's spectral norms need, which LOG-A does not write out: `\u2016N-I\u2016\u2081 \u2264 e^{-2a\u03b8} + e^{-2a(1-\u03b8)} + 4e^{-2a}`. A Decimal fixture checks it at p = 8 (12 cell cuts).\n3. **\u00a73, setup versus online precision.** `a \u2264 16\u2308log\u2082 p\u2309` holds for every p \u2265 3, and `2^{-P_setup} e^{a/(4\u03b8)} < 2^{-Cp}` holds with a 2.77\u00d7 slack. Control: with C = 128, the old Cp-bit weight precision underflows at every p in 32..4096.\n4. **\u00a75, locality.** The stated error `p^10 e^{-p\u00b2}` is exactly right, via the identity `H\u207b\u00b9 \u2212 \u03c3\u03a3_{j<J}Q\u02b2 H\u1d40 = Q^J H\u207b\u00b9`. The identity and the bandwidth `2W(J\u22121)+W` are checked exactly on a banded fixture. The exponents are 40/42/43, below halo 48, below core 128.\n5. **\u00a77, ledger.**\n   - All nine rows were re-derived from the prose table. The minimum is `\u03b5q`, the boundary row is main + 10\u207b\u2076\u2074, and the Gaussian row exceeds main by exactly `\u03b4(1\u22122q)`.\n   - The chirp guard is 0.1841409904237, and the gain over #1758 is 9.279348\u00b710\u207b\u2079.\n   - Rejecting controls: the old \u03b8 ~ 1/d guard, a \u03b8 ~ 1/p guard, \u03b2 = 1\u2212\u03b4/2, and \u03b5 = 1.\n6. **Saturation.** On this nine-row ledger every parameter choice has \u03ba < \u03b5q < q < b_cert = 0.001679754956125544521335, PR1699's certified complex endpoint. Checked along \u03b4 = 10\u207b\u2074..10\u207b\u00b3\u2077. **The outer-only headroom left on this line is (1\u2212\u03b5)q \u2248 1.68\u00b710\u207b\u00b9\u2070.** Further gains need a better certified complex supplier (#1786 Open question 3).\n\n## Not checked\n\n- The SHALLOW-TOEPLITZ and accretive circuit theorem (#1758 \u00a74).\n- The derivation of each cost row's exponent.\n- The union schedule and microbox layout.\n- \u00a74's normalization, beyond its `O(d log p) = o(p)` arithmetic.\n- Supplier admission (no native replay).\n- The all-size compiler and the other inherited hypotheses that #1786 lists.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/pr1786-fine-prime-transfer-audit --check-only\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/pr1786-fine-prime-transfer-audit\n```\n\nBoth commands pass; the verifier passes on Python 3.10, 3.12 and 3.14. `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_research_*.py'` gives 42 tests OK (2 skipped). The base is main `0b1cccf8`. The audited sources are #1786 `c52345ca`, #1673 `2569871f` and #1758 `8d975b6c`, by SHA256 (listed in the README).\n\n## Task card\n\n- Chooser seed `07c595761654b99241c97a49590e2205`: independent-verification / `independent-moment`.\n- Scope **changed**: the selected ledger is already covered by #1293, #1577, #1632 and others, so this audits the newest pending pricing claim.\n- Claim: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1166#discussioncomment-18921325\n\n## Credit\n\n- The audited mathematics is by Chafik Boukhalfa (#1786, with OpenAI Codex), Vlado Vojdanovski (#1673), and IdeaOuter and the #1758 contributors.\n- Tim Trudgian proved the cited prime theorem.\n- The supplier lineage is retained by #1699.\n\nThis audit was prepared end to end by Claude Code (Anthropic Claude Opus) in a session donated by @JosieElliston, with no human review. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
